/-!
# T3B-R's per-member conclusion for a GIVEN export packet (lane FC39-BQ2; review 54 §6.4)

External review 54, §6.4: the per-sequence records must keep the SAME packet — the export packet
`P` with `P.cusp = B`, its levels (cusp piece `= {level ≤ 90}`, defining function `= level − 90`)
and the product-or-separation alternative of T3 for THIS packet. `BoundaryPacketsOutBFR_BQ`
(FC39-BQ, verbatim T3B-R) hides `P` behind an existential; this file splits it:

* `BoundaryPacketRestBFR_BQ2 W g K A δn idx … P` — everything after `∃ P, P.cusp = B ∧`
  (verbatim; generated by `build-logs/scratch/FC39-BQ2/gen_rest.py` from the accepted text);
* `boundaryPacketsOutBFR_iff_rest_BQ2` — `BoundaryPacketsOutBFR_BQ … ↔ ∃ P, P.cusp = B ∧ Rest P`
  (definitional).
* Consumers: `BoundaryPacketRestBFR_BQ2.ratio_le_BQ2` (T3B's cusp-tolerance clause),
  `BoundaryPacketRestBFR_BQ2.alternative_BQ2` (T3's labelled whole-product branch OR the separation
  of the enlarged collars and level sets, for the given packet).
-/

